00:02:31.019 --> 00:02:34.560
should add up to 65, all right. How do

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:35.819
you work out the magic number? What we're

00:02:35.819 --> 00:02:38.189
going to do is add up all the numbers in

00:02:38.189 --> 00:02:39.659
the square, all right? So it's gonna be

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:42.150
1 plus 2 plus 3 plus 4, right. So we

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:45.209
get 1 plus 2 plus 3 plus- and so

00:02:45.209 --> 00:02:47.700
on. And that will go up to- well the

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.659
biggest num- if it was nxn it

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:56.669
goes up to n squared. 
So we're going to add up all

00:02:56.669 --> 00:02:58.349
these numbers together; so they go all

00:02:58.349 --> 00:03:01.049
the way up to n squared, so n squared

00:03:01.049 --> 00:03:04.319
would be 9 here. It would be 16 here and

00:03:04.319 --> 00:03:07.859
it's 25 here. So we're going to
add them all

00:03:07.859 --> 00:03:09.840
together; there's a nice little trick

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.879
to do that which is very simple to

00:03:11.879 --> 00:03:14.579
explain. If you add the first number and

00:03:14.579 --> 00:03:17.370
the last number together what do I get? I

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:22.650
get n squared plus 1. If I add the second

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:24.720
number and the second to last you get

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:27.239
the same thing, n squared plus 1. You can

00:03:27.239 --> 00:03:28.949
actually add them up in pairs, you always

00:03:28.949 --> 00:03:31.229
get the same value. How many pairs are

00:03:31.229 --> 00:03:35.629
there? It's n squared divided by 2 pairs.

00:03:35.629 --> 00:03:39.150
So that's how much we get. But if we look

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:40.620
at this in a different way, we're going

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:41.750
to come at this from a different angle,

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:45.690
what about this? We know each row is

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:48.060
equal to the magic number, right, we'll

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:51.000
call it M. So this is equal to M. The

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.400
second row is equal to M, the third row

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.650
is equal to M; every row is equal to the

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:57.989
magic number. How many rows are there?

00:03:57.989 --> 00:04:01.470
Well there's n of them. So if you add all

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:03.269
this together, another way of thinking

00:04:03.269 --> 00:04:06.689
about that is it's n lots of the magic

00:04:06.689 --> 00:04:08.729
number. And that means we can work out

00:04:08.729 --> 00:04:10.979
what the magic number is; if I do that

00:04:10.979 --> 00:04:13.379
using this that must mean the magic

00:04:13.379 --> 00:04:17.940
number is - we just divide 
look - it's going

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:21.599
to be n divided by 2 times n squared

00:04:21.599 --> 00:04:23.669
plus 1. So we learn how to do the magic

00:04:23.669 --> 00:04:24.930
number, look let's do it! And let's have

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:27.210
this one, n equals 3,

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:33.100
the magic 
number is: 9, 3 squared equals 9,

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:38.710
plus 1 is 10 and times by 3 is 30, divided

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:41.740
by 2 is 15 - that's how you work out the

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:44.740
magic number, yeah. So a
kind of nice little

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:46.000
thing about maths there is looking at the

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:47.380
same problem in two different ways to

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:49.030
